===Etymology===
{{multiple images
|direction = vertical
|image1 = OmahaKiewitPlaza.jpg
|caption1 = {{w|Kiewit Plaza}} in [[Omaha]], [[Nebraska]], USA, the [[corporate#Adjective|corporate]] [[headquarters]] of {{w|Berkshire Hathaway}}, a [[multinational]] conglomerate ''(sense 2)''
|image2 = Conglomerate rock called puddingstone. - geograph.org.uk - 480555.jpg
|caption2 = A close-up view of the largest of [[w:Trellech#Harold's Stones|Harold’s Stones]] in {{w|Trellech}}, [[Monmouthshire]], [[Wales]], UK, composed of [[puddingstone]] which is a kind of conglomerate ''(sense 3)''
}}

From {{der|en|la|conglomerātus}}, {{glossary|past}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|conglomerāre||to pile into a heap, to roll together}}, from {{m|la|con-||''prefix indicating a being or bringing together of several objects''}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ḱóm||beside, by, near, with}}) + {{m|la|glomerāre}} (from {{m|la|glomerō||to pile into a heap, to make into a ball, glomerate}}, from {{m|la|glomus||ball of thread; ball-shaped mass}},<ref>{{R:Oxford English Dictionary|entry=Conglomerate|part of speech=''v.''|volume=II|page=822|column=1}}</ref> from {{der|en|ine-pro|*gel-||to form into a ball; ball}}).

